   {
    "text": "*Summer Days in the Countryside*  \n\n*(Verse 1)*  \nI used to wake up in the morning with the sun,  \nA golden light that painted the sky in blue.  \nThe fields were green, the air was fresh and pure,  \nAnd the scent of wildflowers, it was so true.  \n\nMy toes would touch the earth, the grass was soft,  \nI’d chase the clouds and laugh with the wind.  \nThe creek would sing, the trees would sway and dance,  \nAnd the world felt like it was just meant to be.  \n\n*(Chorus)*  \nOh, summer days in the countryside,  \nWhere the memories are so deep and true.  \nThe laughter, the songs, the quiet peace,  \nA time I’ll always cherish, in my heart.  \n\n*(Verse 2)*  \nI’d build my forts in the meadow’s edge,  \nWith sticks and leaves, and dreams that never fade.  \nThe fireflies would light up the night,  \nAnd the stars would shine like they’d been made.  \n\nI’d ride my bike through the fields and woods,  \nWhere the world was wide and the sky was bold.  \nThe scent of pine, the sound of birds,  \nAnd the freedom that came with the bold.  \n\n*(Chorus)*  \nOh, summer days in the countryside,  \nWhere the memories are so deep and true.  \nThe laughter, the songs, the quiet peace,  \nA time I’ll always cherish, in my heart.  \n\n*(Bridge)*  \nNow I’m far from the hills and the fields,  \nBut the memories still stay in my mind.  \nThe warmth of the sun, the cool of the breeze,  \nAnd the love that was shared in the breeze.  \n\n*(Outro)*  \nSo here’s to the summers of my childhood,  \nIn the countryside, where I was born.  \nWith every memory, I’ll always keep,  \nThe love and the joy that I’ve been given.",
